	<key>readme</key>
	<string># Aeye 🦉

Show **Cursor** and **Claude** usage toward plan limits from Alfred.

More info: https://github.com/giovannicoppola/alfred-aeye

## Setup
- For Cursor rows: signed in to the Cursor app on this Mac
- For Claude rows: Claude Code signed in (OAuth in Keychain)
- Optional: change the keyword below (default: `!e`), or assign a hotkey
- Optional: uncheck rows you don’t use (Composer/Auto, Other models, Hourly, Weekly)

## Usage
1. Type the keyword → enabled rows (Composer/Auto, Other models, Hourly, Weekly)
2. Results are cached for ~60s

### Reading the rows
- Circle meter: 🟢 → 🟡 → 🔴 as you approach the limit (⚪ unused)
- **Composer / Auto** / **Other models** — same split as the Cursor spending page
- Cursor `$x / $y` = included compute spend vs plan included limit (not necessarily billed $)
- `(🕐 68%, 11d, Tue Aug 21)` = % of period elapsed, then time until reset (`d` / `h` / `m`)
- Pace emoji after the parenthesis: 🐢 underspending · 🎯 on track · 🔥 overspending (spent % vs elapsed %)
- `(🕐 40%, 5h, 11:30pm)` on Hourly when a session is active
- **Hourly** — Claude 5-hour session limit (Claude Code icon)
- **Weekly** — Claude weekly limit
- Claude `experimental` = % from Anthropic’s OAuth usage API (not official statusline)

## Actions
- ⏎: copy the selected row
- ⌘⏎: open the service dashboard</string>
